# Test Agent

## Purpose

Before building the main multi-agent system, a simplified test agent was built to validate the core architecture. The test agent proved that the end-to-end pattern works — agent reads from knowledge source, generates content, calls flow, flow populates Word template, saves to SharePoint, returns URL.

This validated the pattern before investing in the full four-agent system.

---

## What the Test Agent Does

1. Reads a fixed test file (`Test_AG_File.docx`) from the knowledge source
2. Generates a one-paragraph summary of its content
3. Captures today's date
4. Calls the flow with two variables: `SummaryDate` and `SummaryContent`
5. The flow populates a two-field Word template and saves to SharePoint
6. Returns the SharePoint URL to the user

---

## What the Test Proved

| Component | Validated |
|---|---|
| Agent reads from SharePoint knowledge source | ✅ |
| Agent generates content and stores in named variables | ✅ |
| Agent calls flow tool automatically (no user prompt) | ✅ |
| Flow receives named variables from agent | ✅ |
| Flow populates Word template with Content Controls | ✅ |
| Flow saves file to SharePoint with timestamped name | ✅ |
| Flow returns URL to agent | ✅ |
| Agent returns URL to user | ✅ |

---

## Key Lessons That Shaped the Main Architecture

**Tool description wording is everything.** The first tool description ("imports material into a Word template and publishes") caused the agent to ask the user to provide the report content. The corrected description — specifying when to call, what to pass, and not to ask the user — caused the agent to call the tool automatically with the correct input.

**Variable names must be consistent.** `SummaryDate` and `SummaryContent` were used consistently across: agent instructions, flow trigger input names, and the tool description. Any mismatch caused the tool call to fail or pass wrong values.

**Topics are not needed for single-intent agents.** An attempt was made to wrap the agent in a topic for "more control." Testing showed the generative orchestrator bypassed the topic and handled the request directly — correctly and reliably. The topic was disabled.

**`body/lastResponse` is the correct output path.** `body/responses` (an array) returned inconsistent results. `body/lastResponse` (a string) reliably contains the agent's final text response.

